    {
      "archive": "mods\\TConstruct-1.20.1-3.11.2.166.jar",
      "path": "assets/tconstruct/book/mighty_smelting/en_us/tools/designing.json",
      "fields": [
        {
          "field": "title",
          "value": "Designing Tools"
        },
        {
          "field": "text",
          "value": "Stuck on design? Let me teach you the Thruul method! Start with a goal: want a strong melee weapon? ore miner? wither killer? The more precise your goal the stronger the tool."
        },
        {
          "field": "text",
          "value": "Next, identify the most important stats and modifiers to the goal. For melee, might be damage or damage per second. Ore mining may want luck or mining speed. Don't forget \"deal breakers\", like if you need cheap repair."
        },
        {
          "field": "text",
          "value": "Finally, match tool type, materials, and modifiers to whats important. For materials, check the tip icon in the top corner. Also remember conditional modifiers like smite may be stronger than simple stat boosts if you can meet their conditions."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "archive": "mods\\TConstruct-1.20.1-3.11.2.166.jar",
      "path": "assets/tconstruct/book/mighty_smelting/en_us/tools/tips.json",
      "fields": [
        {
          "field": "title",
          "value": "Tool Tips"
        },
        {
          "field": "text",
          "value": "Alright Tinker, you are about to learn about one of the most powerful ways to improve tools, abilities. Before you do, let me give you some quick advice."
        },
        {
          "field": "text",
          "value": "First, you might think the goal of tinkering is to create the best tool, but its not! Your goal is to make a good tool, and its hard to fail that. You can always improve your tool later."
        },
        {
          "field": "text",
          "value": "Also, you might be wondering, \"Is something worth using?\". Simple! Just try them all! If you hate it, you can always recycle the tool, or just hide it in a chest. No rush to try each modifier, just start with what sounds fun!"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "archive": "mods\\TConstruct-1.20.1-3.11.2.166.jar",
      "path": "assets/tconstruct/book/tinkers_gadgetry/en_us/exploration/cobalt_shard.json",
      "fields": [
        {
          "field": "title",
          "value": "Cobalt Shards"
        },
        {
          "field": "text",
          "value": "Cobalt shards cannot be found from slimes, only appearing in ichor geodes. They are primarily useful as an alternative source of the ore."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "archive": "mods\\TConstruct-1.20.1-3.11.2.166.jar",
      "path": "assets/tconstruct/book/mighty_smelting/en_us/tools/tanks.json",
      "fields": [
        {
          "field": "title",
          "value": "Tool Tanks"
        },
        {
          "field": "text",
          "value": "Modifiers such as spitting, melting, and smashing will give the tool a tank. Fluid can be inserted or extracted by interacting with a tank while holding the tool. You can also fill and empty it in the smeltery GUI using the bucket slot (4) or by clicking a fluid in the tank (2) with the tool."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "archive": "mods\\TConstruct-1.20.1-3.11.2.166.jar",
      "path": "assets/tconstruct/book/tinkers_gadgetry/en_us/exploration/cobalt_ore.json",
      "fields": [
        {
          "field": "title",
          "value": "Cobalt Ore"
        },
        {
          "field": "text",
          "value": "Cobalt ore can be found scattered around the nether. It is most common near ancient debris between elevations of 8 and 32, though it can be located at any height in smaller quantities. Since the ore often appears exposed to air, it can often be easily spotted by its distinct hue in the walls or ceiling of the Nether."
        }
      ]
    }
